346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (The project is about using Prolog language to plan a trip between specific cities such as Cairo, Alexandria, Aswan, and Hurghada using available modes of transportation like trains, planes, and cars. The program uses a database and specific rules to reach the designated city either directly or indirectly through recursion. It can utilize one or multiple modes of transportation and tries to find a way to reach the target city. The program will print the route from one city to another using one or more modes of transport. If it finds another route, it will print it, and if no route is available, it will print a message stating that it cannot reach the destination.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
